cells:
  - kind: 1
    value: "# Section 7: Single-Row Functions\r

      ## Single Row Functions\r

      ### What is a Function?\r

      - are created for manipulating the data and returning a value\r

      - must be created before calling them. Otherwise, you will have the
      following error:\r

      \  - 'Function has not been defined yet!'\r

      - are formerly created codes that reside in the database. can be called
      easily by typing only their names and parameters\r

      - is a bunch of code created for reuse\r

      - two types of functions:\r

      \  1. single-row\r

      \  2. multiple-row\r

      \r

      ![types of functions](types_of_functions.png)\r

      ### Single-Row Functions\r

      - operate on single rows and return only one result per row\r

      - accept one or more arguments and return one value\r

      - return value for each row returned\r

      - can be used alone or nested\r

      \  - function1(function2(function3(x)))\r

      - column or an expression can be used as arguments\r

      - returning data types can be different than the input data types\r

      - can be used in SELECT, WHERE, or ORDER BY clauses\r

      \  - ```SQL \r

      \    SELECT function_name[(arg1, arg2, ...)] FROM dual;\r

      \    ```\r

      - are categorized by the data types of their input parameters\r

      - **character functions**-accept character values as input, and return
      character or numeric values\r

      - **number fucntions**-accept numeric values as input & return numeric
      values as output\r

      - **date functions**-operate on values of the DATE data type\r

      - **conversion functions**-used to convert one data type to another\r

      \  - ![conversion function](conversion_function.png)\r

      - **general functions**-take in any data type. But, they are mainly used
      to handle the NULL values\r

      ### Character Functions\r

      - take in character data as input & return character or numeric data as
      output\r

      - two different types of character functions:\r

      \  1. **Case conversion functions:** convert characters to upper case or
      lower case\r

      \     - UPPER function\r

      \     - LOWER function\r

      \     - INITCAP function\r

      \  2. **Character manipulation functions:**\r

      \     - SUBSTR function\r

      \     - LENGTH function\r

      \     - CONCAT function\r

      \     - INSTR function\r

      \     - TRIM function\r

      \     - REPLACE function\r

      \     - LPAD/RPAD function"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      SELECT first_name, SUBSTR(first_name, 3, 6), SUBSTR(first_name, 3),\r

      \    last_name, LENGTH(last_name)\r

      FROM employees;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      SELECT CONCAT(first_name, last_name)\r

      FROM employees;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      SELECT CONCAT(CONCAT(first_name, last_name), employee_id)\r

      FROM employees;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      SELECT first_name || last_name || employee_id\r

      FROM employees;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      SELECT INSTR('I am learning how to use functions in Oracle', 'o', 17, 3)\r

      FROM dual;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      SELECT INSTR('I am learning how to use functions in Oracle', 'o', 1, 3)\r

      FROM dual;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      SELECT INSTR('I am learning how to use functions in Oracle', 'o', -1, 3)\r

      FROM duals;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      SELECT INSTR('I am learning how to use funtions in Oracle', 'o', -1, 1)\r

      FROM dual;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      SELECT INSTR('I am learning how to use functions in Oracle', 'in', -1,
      1)\r

      FROM dual;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      SELECT INSTR('I am learning how to use functions in Oracle', 'in', 1, 1)\r

      FROM dual;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      SELECT TRIM('    My name is Adam   ') trm from dual;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      SELECT TRIM (''FROM'    My Name is Adam  ') trm from dual;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      SELECT TRIM(BOTH''FROM'     My Name is Adam   ') trm from dual;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      SELECT TRIM(LEADING''FROM'    My Name is Adam  ') trm from dual;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      SELECT TRIM(TRAILING ''FROM'    My Name is Adam   ') trm\r

      from dual;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r\n"
    languageId: oracle-sql
